DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       These macros define and operate on doubly linked circular queues.

       In the macro definitions, _T_Y_P_E is the name of a user‐defined structure,
       that must contain a field of type _C_I_R_C_L_E_Q___E_N_T_R_Y, named _N_A_M_E.  The argu‐
       ment _H_E_A_D_N_A_M_E is the name of a user‐defined structure that must be  de‐
       clared using the macro CCIIRRCCLLEEQQ__HHEEAADD().

   CCrreeaattiioonn
       A circular queue is headed by a structure defined by the CCIIRRCCLLEEQQ__HHEEAADD()
       macro.   This  structure  contains a pair of pointers, one to the first
       element in the queue and the other to the last element  in  the  queue.
       The  elements are doubly linked so that an arbitrary element can be re‐
       moved without traversing the queue.  New elements can be added  to  the
       queue  after  an  existing  element, before an existing element, at the
       head of the queue, or at the end of the queue.  A  _C_I_R_C_L_E_Q___H_E_A_D  struc‐
       ture is declared as follows:

           CIRCLEQ_HEAD(HEADNAME, TYPE) head;

       where  _s_t_r_u_c_t  _H_E_A_D_N_A_M_E is the structure to be defined, and _s_t_r_u_c_t _T_Y_P_E
       is the type of the elements to be linked into the queue.  A pointer  to
       the head of the queue can later be declared as:

           struct HEADNAME *headp;

       (The names _h_e_a_d and _h_e_a_d_p are user selectable.)

       CCIIRRCCLLEEQQ__EENNTTRRYY()  declares a structure that connects the elements in the
       queue.

       CCIIRRCCLLEEQQ__HHEEAADD__IINNIITTIIAALLIIZZEERR() evaluates to an initializer  for  the  queue
       _h_e_a_d.

       CCIIRRCCLLEEQQ__IINNIITT() initializes the queue referenced by _h_e_a_d.

       CCIIRRCCLLEEQQ__EEMMPPTTYY() evaluates to true if there are no items on the queue.

   IInnsseerrttiioonn
       CCIIRRCCLLEEQQ__IINNSSEERRTT__HHEEAADD()  inserts  the  new element _e_l_m at the head of the
       queue.

       CCIIRRCCLLEEQQ__IINNSSEERRTT__TTAAIILL() inserts the new element _e_l_m at  the  end  of  the
       queue.

       CCIIRRCCLLEEQQ__IINNSSEERRTT__BBEEFFOORREE()  inserts the new element _e_l_m before the element
       _l_i_s_t_e_l_m.

       CCIIRRCCLLEEQQ__IINNSSEERRTT__AAFFTTEERR() inserts the new element _e_l_m  after  the  element
       _l_i_s_t_e_l_m.

   TTrraavveerrssaall
       CCIIRRCCLLEEQQ__FFIIRRSSTT() returns the first item on the queue.

       CCIIRRCCLLEEQQ__LLAASSTT() returns the last item on the queue.

       CCIIRRCCLLEEQQ__PPRREEVV() returns the previous item on the queue, or _&_h_e_a_d if this
       item is the first one.

       CCIIRRCCLLEEQQ__NNEEXXTT()  returns  the  next  item on the queue, or _&_h_e_a_d if this
       item is the last one.

       CCIIRRCCLLEEQQ__LLOOOOPP__PPRREEVV() returns the previous item on the queue.  If _e_l_m  is
       the first element on the queue, the last element is returned.

       CCIIRRCCLLEEQQ__LLOOOOPP__NNEEXXTT()  returns the next item on the queue.  If _e_l_m is the
       last element on the queue, the first element is returned.

       CCIIRRCCLLEEQQ__FFOORREEAACCHH() traverses the queue referenced by _h_e_a_d in the forward
       direction, assigning each element in turn to _v_a_r.  _v_a_r is set to  _&_h_e_a_d
       if the loop completes normally, or if there were no elements.

       CCIIRRCCLLEEQQ__FFOORREEAACCHH__RREEVVEERRSSEE() traverses the queue referenced by _h_e_a_d in the
       reverse direction, assigning each element in turn to _v_a_r.

   RReemmoovvaall
       CCIIRRCCLLEEQQ__RREEMMOOVVEE() removes the element _e_l_m from the queue.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       CCIIRRCCLLEEQQ__EEMMPPTTYY()  returns nonzero if the queue is empty, and zero if the
       queue contains at least one entry.

       CCIIRRCCLLEEQQ__FFIIRRSSTT(),   CCIIRRCCLLEEQQ__LLAASSTT(),   CCIIRRCCLLEEQQ__LLOOOOPP__PPRREEVV(),   and    CCIIRR‐‐
       CCLLEEQQ__LLOOOOPP__NNEEXXTT() return a pointer to the first, last, previous, or next
       _T_Y_P_E structure, respectively.

       CCIIRRCCLLEEQQ__PPRREEVV(),   and   CCIIRRCCLLEEQQ__NNEEXXTT()   are   similar  to  their  CCIIRR‐‐
       CCLLEEQQ__LLOOOOPP__**() counterparts, except that if the argument is the first or
       last element, respectively, they return _&_h_e_a_d.

       CCIIRRCCLLEEQQ__HHEEAADD__IINNIITTIIAALLIIZZEERR() returns an initializer that can be  assigned
       to the queue _h_e_a_d.

